(footprint "Relay_SPST_RelComm_RSS-SR042P"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "manual")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "RelComm RSS-SR042P SPST RF reed relay, MIL-grade coaxial package.  Metal body/base = ground return; sits flat on a solid PCB ground pad.  Base is 25.4 mm (1.0 in) long by 8.64 mm (0.34 in) wide; total length 30.48 mm (1.2 in) including the two axial RF pins protruding 2.54 mm beyond each end of the base.  Height above PCB = 25.4 mm (1.0 in) to top of coil housing (vertical clearance).  Coil housing is a fat-T stem extending from one long edge of the base: 14.48 mm (0.57 in) wide (centered on the long axis of the base) and 17.78 mm (0.7 in) deep, cantilevered off the NEAR long edge in the -Y direction.  The far edge of the coil is ~26 mm (~1.0 in) from the far long edge of the base.  Courtyard reserves this stem zone -- do NOT place components under the coil housing.  Note: the overhang is ONE-SIDED (not symmetric) so you can pack components close to the FAR long edge of the base.  Two mounting screws (approx 6-32, verify at hardware store) through the base at 0.68 in (17.27 mm) spacing along the long axis, offset 0.2 in (5.08 mm) from the side opposite the coil connector.  PCB mounting holes are 4.0 mm NPTH (oversize relative to the 3.5 mm 6-32 OD) to tolerate measurement uncertainty on screw spacing.  RF path: single-pole single-throw, 50 ohm nominal, VSWR <= 1.1:1 to 26.5 GHz, 500 W below 100 MHz.  Coil: 28 V nominal, exits top of body via a small latching plastic connector.  The user plan is to cut that connector off and route each relay's coil wires to a separate 2-pin screw terminal placed elsewhere on the PCB; the coil connection is therefore NOT part of this footprint.  Only three pads here: RF_A (1), RF_B (2), and SHIELD/base-ground (3).  RF pins are elevated above the PCB; connect each via a short jumper wire from the SMD RF landing pad to the pin tip.  Datasheet retrieved to storage; parameters recorded in memory reference_relays_rss_sr042p.")
	(tags "relay reed SPST RF RelComm RSS RSS-SR042P junkbox")
